b. take first action at that time at the scene and conduct examination; c. interrogate a suspect and examine the suspect's identity;
d. seize objects and/or letters; e. take fingerprints and photograph a person; f. summon persons to be heard and examined as suspects or witnesses;
g. bring in experts needed in connection with the examination of the case;
h. terminate the investigation after receiving instructions from the General Investigator that there is insufficient evidence, or the incident does not constitute a criminal act and subsequently through the General Investigator notify this matter to the public prosecutor, the suspect or their family; and/or
i. take other actions necessary for the smooth investigation of criminal acts of violence against women and children, which according to law can be legally accounted for.
(3) Investigators as referred to in paragraph (2), notify the commencement of the investigation and submit the results of their investigation to the public prosecutor through the Investigating Officer of the Police of the Republic of Indonesia, in accordance with the provisions stipulated in the Criminal Procedure Law. v;

Article 4

Every woman and child who becomes a victim of physical, psychological violence, exploitation or human trafficking is entitled to protection and services.

Protection, assistance, and services for victims as referred to in paragraph (1) include:

a. to be respected for their dignity as human beings;
b. complaints or requests for protection from the concerned party and/or other parties; c. confidential handling or placement of victims in safe locations and houses whose whereabouts are kept secret to avoid intimidation and threats;

medical services/health care in the form of d. treatment and recovery of injuries or physical condition of victims by medical and paramedical personnel; medicolegal services for evidentiary purposes e. in the legal field; protection by law enforcement officials; f. provision of information regarding legal rights and obligations ob. to victims or guardians of victims as well as identification of incidents; continuous handling up to the stage h.

