1. as well as sexual health according to the suffering experienced by victims of violence; psychological assistance to J. restore the traumatic condition of victims and restore victims' self-confidence;

k. assistance for legal processes and obtaining compensation or compensation rights; 1. provision of spiritual guidance services;

m. to make their own decisions;

n. assistance by social workers and legal aid at every level of the examination process in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations;

i. guarantees of rights related to status as family members and community members (social reintegration); and L -D-F {,

