Article 6

The obligations and responsibilities of the Regional Government as referred to in Article 5 letter a, include: a. implementing the obligations for protection of women and children from acts of violence established by the government; establishing policies, programs and activities b. for protection of women and children from acts of violence; conducting cooperation in the implementation c. of protection of women and children from acts of violence;

d. e. providing support for facilities and infrastructure for the implementation of protection of women and children from acts of violence; providing Safe Houses for women and children victims of violence;

f. allocating budget for the implementation of protection of women and children from acts of violence according to regional financial capacity; and

g. fostering and supervising the implementation of protection of women and children from acts of violence;

h. establishing regional technical implementing units for protection of women and children based on the provisions of laws and regulations.

Article 16

(1) The Regional Government through the Dinas/UPTD is obligated to conduct economic empowerment for victims of acts of violence, exploitation and neglect.

(2) Forms of empowerment for victims of acts of violence as referred to in paragraph (1), include:

a. procuring the necessary requirements for entrepreneurship training for victims of acts of violence, to improve business knowledge, attitude, and skills;
b. facilitating the implementation of various job training and skills training;
c. providing assistance in developing productive economic businesses;
d. exploring cooperation with small, medium and large enterprises, as well as financial institutions to develop businesses of victims of acts of violence;
e. endeavoring to provide capital for victims of acts of violence; and
f. expanding information access and promoting the products of victims of acts of violence.
